{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790361395,"nonce":"2Zzjdt2zQ8rIbdyGapJR4u4XFuM=","title":"Handler state is released without dropping its fields","message":"A `with H { }` scope frees its `H$state` region with `Intrinsic::Free` on each exit edge (`LoweringContext::lower_with_scopes`, crates/compiler/src/lowering.rs), and host-owned instances free theirs through `effect_runtime::free_handler_state` (crates/zyntax_embed/src/effect_runtime.rs). Both release the raw region only. A field that owns something (a `Fiber\u003cT\u003e`, a list, a string, a boxed value) leaks when the scope or the instance ends.\n\nWhat exists: `H$state` is an ordinary `@reference` struct registered by `synthesize_handler_state`, and crates/compiler/src/drop_glue.rs already synthesizes field-releasing functions for `@reference` types with reference fields.\n\nDone: leaving a `with` scope and reaping a host handler instance both run the state struct's field release before freeing the region, and a test holds a fiber in handler state across a scope without leaking it.","files":null}]}